# -- SsaCore.xcframework: Kotlin/Native stdlib cache, simulator slice only (audit a)
# `xcrun objdump --reloc` puts all 11 _dlsym call sites of this member (offsets
# 0x76a320-0x76a528) inside _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication
# (0x76a1b8-0x76a900), the runtime's stack-trace symbolicator; the archive
# holds the strings CoreSymbolication.framework/CoreSymbolication and
# CSSymbolicatorCreateWithPid. The device slice does not define that function.
SsaCore.xcframework/ios-arm64-simulator/SsaCore.framework/SsaCore(libstdlib-cache.a.o) _dlsym Kotlin/Native stdlib: all 11 call sites are in _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication (stack-trace symbolication via CoreSymbolication), simulator slice only

# -- Test bundles that link SsaCore statically (audit c) -----------------------
# Each bundle defines _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication, the stdlib
# function above, and no longer contains _platform_posix_dlsym_wrapper50 (the
# linker dropped it). The other static inputs on each link line import no
# _dlsym: the test target's own object (CoreCryptoTests.o, PdfSpikeTests.o),
# CoreCrypto.o or SsaPdf.o (audit b), and the clang profile runtime that
# -profile-generate (code coverage) adds, libclang_rt.profile_iossim.a.
# XCTestSwiftSupport is a dylib. NetworkGuardTests.xctest gets no entry.
CoreCryptoTests.xctest/CoreCryptoTests _dlsym from libSystem; caller is the statically linked Kotlin/Native _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication, not our Swift
SsaPdfTests.xctest/SsaPdfTests _dlsym from libSystem; caller is the statically linked Kotlin/Native _Kotlin_getSourceInfo_core_symbolication, not our Swift

# -- ONNX Runtime 1.22.0 iOS xcframework (Run 8, spike 3b) ----------------------
# prelinked_objects.o is the one merged object in each slice's archive. nm -u shows no
# networking framework, class or symbol in it; _dlsym is the only match, found by objdump -d -r
# on each thinned slice. The maccatalyst slice is not linked by an iOS app and is listed so the
# audit over the whole xcframework passes.
onnxruntime.xcframework/ios-arm64/onnxruntime.framework/onnxruntime(prelinked_objects.o) _dlsym ONNX Runtime 1.22.0 (NuGet Microsoft.ML.OnnxRuntime iOS build): the only caller, in every slice and architecture, is onnxruntime::(anonymous)::PosixEnv::GetSymbolFromLibrary, which looks a symbol up in a library that was loaded with dlopen (custom-op and execution-provider libraries); our code loads none, to be re-checked when :models links it
